('hr-ref-074','I am looking for a role where I can grow and contribute over time. If the work and expectations remain a good fit, I would be glad to build a long-term record here.',null,null,null),
('hr-ref-075','I may bring experience beyond some requirements, but I am interested in the actual work and scope. I would like to understand how the team can use that experience without assuming a title or promotion.',null,null,null),
('hr-ref-076','No. I would explain the concern, suggest accurate wording, and escalate if someone insisted on a false statement. Trust is harder to rebuild than a difficult conversation.',null,null,null),
('hr-ref-077','The toughest decision was [specific choice] under [constraint]. I compared the options, consulted [relevant people], chose [action], and learned [lesson] from the outcome.',null,null,null),
('hr-ref-078','I asked what my manager wanted to review and agreed on checkpoints. I kept the work visible, incorporated feedback quickly, and earned more autonomy by delivering consistently.',null,null,null),
('hr-ref-079','I ask how each person prefers to communicate and agree on shared deliverables. Different styles are useful when we keep decisions and ownership explicit.',null,null,null),
('hr-ref-080','My ideal job lets me solve [kind of problem], work with [team style], and see [impact]. This role appeals to me because [verified overlap with the position].',null,null,null),
('hr-ref-081','The achievement with the greatest impact was [project]. My contribution was [action], and it improved [measured outcome]; I am proud of how the team worked together.',null,null,null),
('hr-ref-082','I care about producing something useful and reliable. Seeing [user or team benefit] from [past work] is a strong reason for me to do the job well.',null,null,null),
('hr-ref-083','I ask for examples, separate the feedback from my identity, and decide what to change. After [feedback], I tried [action] and checked whether [result] improved.',null,null,null),
